Subject: [PATCH 7/8] sbr_hfadj: hf_assembly four QMF bands at a time

VibeSDR patch for FAAD2 2.11.3 (the plain build VibeServer links for DAB+ audio, libfaad_dab.a). GPL-2.0-or-later,
as FAAD2. Written for VibeSDR, 2026-10-26; applied by vibeserver/linux/build-deps.sh and vibeserver/mac/build-deps.sh
in the order of faad2-patches/series. Measured on real off-air DAB+ unit logs (HE-AAC v2, 21 logs, 1909 s):
output against stock FAAD2 2.11.3 built with its own flags — see each header for the figures.

The smoothed gains (one five-slot ring for every band), the noise floor from V[] (each band its own index), the
Q = 0 rule where a band carries a sinusoid, and the sinusoid itself, for four bands per pass with the stock arithmetic
per lane. The remainder of fewer than four, and the bitstream's extension 3/42 case, run the stock loop.

--- a/libfaad/sbr_hfadj.c
+++ b/libfaad/sbr_hfadj.c
